r as its own volume, it cannot float. However, when submerged, the bottom part of the ship can create additional empty space under the water, allowing more volume to be submerged and thus greater displacement, enabling it to float. This is how a ship can weigh more than the water it displaces but still float.\n\nContrastingly, a solid steel bolt sinks because it displaces more water than its volume. Water is denser than solid steel. The force of gravity pulling it downward is less than the buoyant force pushing it upward, making the bolt sink. This is because the bolt can only float as long as the buoyant force equals its weight, and since steel is much denser than water, the buoyant force required by the bolt is greater than its own weight.", "tokens": ["A", "Ġsteel", "Ġship", "Ġsinks", "Ġin", "Ġwater", "Ġbecause", "Ġit", "Ġdispl", "aces", "Ġless", "Ġthan", "Ġits", "Ġown", "Ġvolume", ".", "ĠIf", "Ġit", "Ġdispl", "aces", "Ġonly", "Ġas", "Ġmuch", "Ġwater", "Ġas", "Ġits", "Ġown", "Ġvolume", ",", "Ġit", "Ġcannot", "Ġfloat", ".", "ĠHowever", ",", "Ġwhen", "Ġsubmerged", ",", "Ġthe", "Ġbottom", "Ġpart", "Ġof", "Ġthe", "Ġship", "Ġcan", "Ġcreate", "Ġadditional", "Ġempty", "Ġspace", "Ġunder", "Ġthe", "Ġwater", ",", "Ġallowing", "Ġmore", "Ġvolume", "Ġto", "Ġbe", "Ġsubmerged", "Ġand", "Ġthus", "Ġgreater", "Ġdisplacement", ",", "Ġenabling", "Ġit", "Ġto", "Ġfloat", ".", "ĠThis", "Ġis", "Ġhow", "Ġa", "Ġship", "Ġcan", "Ġweigh", "Ġmore", "Ġthan", "Ġthe", "Ġwater", "Ġit", "Ġdispl", "aces", "Ġbut", "Ġstill", "Ġfloat", ".ĊĊ", "Contr", "ast", "ingly", ",", "Ġa", "Ġsolid", "Ġsteel", "Ġbolt", "Ġsinks", "Ġbecause", "Ġit", "Ġdispl", "aces", "Ġmore", "Ġwater", "Ġthan", "Ġits", "Ġvolume", ".", "ĠWater", "Ġis", "Ġdens", "er", "Ġthan", "Ġsolid", "Ġsteel", ".", "ĠThe", "Ġforce", "Ġof", "Ġgravity", "Ġpulling", "Ġit", "Ġdownward", "Ġis", "Ġless", "Ġthan", "Ġthe", "Ġbuoy", "ant", "Ġforce", "Ġpushing", "Ġit", "Ġupward", ",", "Ġmaking", "Ġthe", "Ġbolt", "Ġsink", ".", "ĠThis", "Ġis", "Ġbecause", "Ġth